    "approach": {
      "foundation": "What is the current state of the system? What's running, what's healthy, what's vulnerable? The infrastructure itself is the ground truth.",
      "build_up": "From current state, build toward desired state layer by layer. Network → compute → storage → application → monitoring → security. Each layer stands on the one below.",
      "break_down": "When something fails, trace back through the layers. Is it DNS? Network? The application? The database? Peel back until you find the foundation that shifted.",
      "anchor": "The running system. What is actually deployed, actually responding, actually backed up — not what the docs say should be true."
    },
    "learning_style": "Learns infrastructure by operating it — understands failure modes by having survived them. Experience is the teacher.",
    "problem_solving": "Assess → Stabilize → Diagnose → Fix → Verify → Document. Always in that order."
  },

